# Code Quality

Source: `governance/quality/engineering-standards.md`

- Follow the project's existing conventions, structure and style; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Names express intent and domain meaning.
- Reuse existing services/utilities before creating new ones.
- No abstraction, layer or configuration without a present, concrete need.
- Never swallow errors; handle, add context, or propagate. Fail closed on security decisions.
- Never log secrets, tokens, credentials or personal data.
- Keep backward compatibility for APIs unless an ADR says otherwise.
- Document known shortcuts as technical debt in the report; do not hide them.

```ts
// ❌ swallowed error
try { await save(order); } catch {}

// ✅ context + propagate
try { await save(order); }
catch (e) { logger.error('Order save failed', { orderId: order.id }); throw new OrderSaveError(order.id, { cause: e }); }
```

AI-generated code is unverified until validated: verify that imported packages and used APIs exist in the
installed versions (`checklists/ai-generated-code.md`).
